cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this model or its outputs, please cite as follows."
title: "Prospective Impact Models for Public Emergency Codes Deployment"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Public Emergency Codes"
    website: "https://github.com/public-emergency-codes"
date-released: "2026-08-09"
version: "pec-prospective-2026-08-09-r9"
abstract: >-
  Pre-deployment prospective probabilistic models estimating conditional
  outcome distributions under future Public Emergency Codes (PEC) deployment
  scenarios. Includes a mortality planning analysis and a U.S. economic-value
  analysis coupled to the mortality model. The models do not estimate observed
  PEC causal effects; they propagate uncertainty in adoption, reach, technical
  completion, receiving-system compatibility, pathway relevance, clinical
  effects, adverse effects, and economic consequences.
keywords:
  - "public emergency codes"
  - "prospective modeling"
  - "mortality"
  - "economic evaluation"
  - "probabilistic simulation"
  - "Monte Carlo"
